Z||000000||ROB MAC||04-02-2000||09:06 PM||||About once or twice a month my throttle seems to stick and when I try to kick it off it sticks at a higher rev.It stays stuck all day. Next day it's fine.Can a faulty t.p.s. do this intermittently? Or are secret agents tampering with my car to run me off a cliff.An electrical test a couple years ago showed funny voltage reading but I've had no trouble till lately.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||04-02-2000||09:16 PM||||<BR>I'd check the IAC valve.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-02-2000||09:17 PM||||You may want to get some throttle body cleaner and hose down the inside of the TB.  Let it sit for a few minutes and thoroughly clean the inside of the throttle body around the the butterfly.  The clearance is so small between the TB and butterfly, that any dirt can cause the butterfly to stick.  Had this problem with my '87 V6.  ||||reg||14
Z||000003||chris6878||04-02-2000||10:55 PM||||My throttle got stuck once too in my 84 coupe. I was out with my ex-girlfriend and hit the gas hard and then it doesnt stop when i let off the pedal. I had to shut off the engine while on the highway.. come to find it out, my throttle cable had broke.. i was expecting it to break soon from the looks of it...    a few of the strands in the cable where already gone and it was just working on what was left, it would stick every now and then, and then it finally broke.          may not be related to your problem though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>chris||||reg||9
